Part of #389 (QA pages must prove each change with evidence for its type).

## What this is

Step 2 of 6. The QA block in a page's content file gains an `evidence` list. Each entry names one change, its type (animation, model, gameplay, ai, visual or none) and its files. `make_page.py` refuses to build when:
- an animation entry lacks a clip, or a before clip and an after clip;
- a model entry lacks a picture, or a before picture and an after picture;
- a gameplay or ai entry lacks a recording, or a before clip and an after clip;
- a visual entry lacks a picture, or a before picture and an after picture;
- a none entry lacks a reason;
- a named file does not exist;
- the page's text names a screenshot or clip path that the page does not show.

The type is also worked out from the changed files (choice 1A): path patterns in the project's `docs/page-style.json`, with defaults for Unity projects (animator controllers and animation files mean animation, model files mean model, enemy and AI scripts mean ai). A type the changed files imply must have an entry. There is no way to skip this (choice 3A). Every project is checked, whatever its pictures setting says.

## Depends on

The Ophan test case step of #389 (the Ophan page's content becomes a test that must be refused).

## Depended on by

The video clip step (the template shows clips) and the end-of-reply check step, which reads the result this step records.

## Done when

Each refusal above has its own passing `verify.py` case, and the Ophan case is refused for missing evidence.

Created by AJ's agent.

